# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub Linguist: report what was WRITTEN, not what the tools emitted.
#
# Without this file GitHub reported:
#     SourcePawn 62.6%   Verilog 35.4%   Python 2%
#
# None of that is right. build/ is 98.4% of this repository by bytes and every
# byte of it is regenerated by the scripts in scripts/: OpenROM GDS and SPICE
# macros, Yosys gate-level netlists, and tool logs. The hand-written source is
# Python; the deliverable is the Verilog in rtl/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Everything under build/ is tool output, not source.
build/**                linguist-generated=true

# A .sp file here is a SPICE netlist written by the OpenROM compiler.
# Linguist maps .sp to SourcePawn, which is the single biggest reason the
# language bar was wrong.
*.sp                    linguist-generated=true
*.lvs.sp                linguist-generated=true

# Tool transcripts and layout data: not a programming language in any sense.
*.log                   linguist-generated=true
*.gds                   binary
*.lef                   linguist-generated=true
*.hex                   linguist-generated=true

# rtl/ is emitted by scripts/gen_*.py, so it is generated too -- but it is the
# point of the project and someone looking for a Verilog Multiply-Select-Add
# fabric should find it. It stays counted as Verilog, deliberately.

# Binary payloads: never try to diff these.
*.npz                   binary
*.pb                    binary
*.h5                    binary
*.safetensors           binary
*.gds                   -diff

# Generated reports and documents: keep them in the repo, keep them out of the
# language statistics and out of noisy diffs.
reports/*.json          linguist-generated=true
README.md               linguist-documentation=true
FINAL-REPORT.md         linguist-documentation=true
